  "dom_id": "step-q340343",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{{log}_{3}\u2061x}{{x}^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}ln\u20613}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{3}\u2061x=\\frac{ln\u2061x}{ln\u20613}$ and $v={x}^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{xln\u20613}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln\u20613}-\\frac{ln\u2061x}{ln\u20613}\\cdot 2x)}{({x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{x}{ln\u20613}-\\frac{2xln\u2061x}{ln\u20613})}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2xln\u2061x}{{x}^{4}ln\u20613} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(1-2ln\u2061x)}{{x}^{4}ln\u20613} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2ln\u2061x}{{x}^{3}ln\u20613} \\\\  & =(\\,1-2ln\u2061x\\,)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}ln\u20613}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
